concepts.body_md:
Har module ne apne layer ke liye ek checker ship kiya: `check-agents.mjs`, `check-roster-flat.mjs`, `check-mcp-config.mjs`, `check-patches.mjs`, `lint-doctype-json.mjs`, `check-agent-policy.mjs`, `validate-skill-library.mjs`, `check-handoff.mjs`, eval harness. `verify-system.mjs` in sabko chalata hai aur woh cross-layer checks jodta hai jo inme se kisi ke nahi hain:

- har `skills:` entry ek preloadable SKILL.md tak resolve hoti hai; har Claude Code hook script path (settings aur frontmatter) exist karta hai aur har hook event documented hai;
- Frappe permission floor: `site_config.json` aur `common_site_config.json` reads denied, migrate asked, `drop-site` aur `reinstall` denied, koi allow rule nahi jo `console` ya `execute` grant kare;
- workflow step tables sirf roster agents aur existing skills ka naam leti hain; CLAUDE.md `@imports` resolve hote hain;
- **guard reach**: har script jo preloaded skill agent ko chalane ko kehti hai, us agent ka guard pass karti hai. Check `agents/tool-guard.mjs` se real `checkBash` import karta hai aur use `${CLAUDE_SKILL_DIR}` expand karke command deta hai, wahi form jo Claude Code sach mein chalata hai;
- **app**: `hooks.py` `app_name` aur har dotted path, `modules.txt` packages, har `patches.txt` line jo `def execute()` wale module tak resolve ho, har DocType folder `__init__.py`, JSON, controller class (`SL Patient` se `SLPatient`) aur test ke saath;
- **`--bench` ke saath**: `apps/spice_lite` is repo ki app hai, `sites/apps.txt` use list karta hai, `bench --site test.localhost list-apps` use aur uske `required_apps` dikhata hai (shared container mein `flock /tmp/spice-bench.lock` ke under), CLAUDE.md same bench ka naam leti hai, aur har eval hallucination trap `<bench>/apps/frappe` mein false hai.

Is repository par yeh 0 WARN ke saath WIRED report karta hai. Pehle ek report karta tha, aur woh WARN ek real seam tha: `performance-review` ne apne query-count test ke liye `bench --site test.localhost run-tests *` pre-approve kiya tha, lekin sre ka guard `run-tests` block karta hai. Har part apna checker pass karta tha; saath mein, jo sre apni preloaded skill ka step 3.1 follow karta woh exit 2 ke saath block ho jata. Fix ek explicitly liya gaya design decision tha: measurement tester ka kaam hai. `performance-review` ab `bench` pre-approve nahi karti, test khud kabhi nahi chalati, aur tester ke liye apne handoff mein query-count test request daalti hai, taaki sre read-only rahe. Toh practically: `verify-system.mjs` ko CI mein `CI=1 bench --site test.localhost run-tests --app spice_lite` ke bagal mein chalao, aur FAIL row ko broken build treat karo.
